{
  "brief": "STUDIO OM is a contemporary architecture studio working across architecture, interior architecture, adaptive reuse, residential and small-scale public projects, and conceptual research. The identity should feel precise, quiet, material and rigorous \u2014 intellectual rather than corporate, contextual rather than signature, and contemporary without being trendy.",
  "source": "rules",
  "confidence": 0.8500000000000001,
  "rationale": "The brief reads as precise, civic, experimental, material. A Inter sets the text because a neutral face lets the drawing be the thing that is looked at, and the accent #6b6f76 is low-chroma for the same reason: on a technical sheet a saturated accent competes with the linework. Renders default to documentary. Line weights are the ADOS tiers, unchanged \u2014 the hierarchy is derived from how far an element is from the cut plane, not from house style.",
  "assumptions": [
    "line weights defaulted to the ADOS tiers (0.70 / 0.35 / 0.18); a practice with a heavier hand should raise the cut weight"
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Is a typeface already licensed? Every point size is derived from its measured cap height.",
    "Is there an existing mark to carry forward, or is this a new identity?"
  ],
